the macro call a function and have the engine include _inside_ a cpp, so there's no need for extra includes at the call site.\r\n\r\nCalling a function means that the engine include can go in the `error_macros.cpp` instead of the call site. Something like this (untested pseudo code):\r\n\r\n```\r\n#if defined(TOOLS_ENABLED) && defined(DEBUG_ENABLED)\r\n#define PER_PHYSICS_TICK_ALLOCATION_WARNING(m_class) \\\r\nstatic uint64_t consecutive_allocs = 0;\\\r\nstatic uint64_t last_alloc_tick = UINT64_MAX;\\\r\n\t_per_physics_tick_allocation_warning(m_class::get_class_static(), consecutive_allocs, last_alloc_tick)\r\n#else\r\n#define PER_PHYSICS_TICK_ALLOCATION_WARNING(m_class)\r\n#endif\r\n\r\nvoid _per_physics_tick_allocation_warning(StringName p_class_name uint64_t &r_consecutive_allocs, uint64_t &r_last_alloc_tick);\r\n\r\n...\r\ncpp:\r\n\r\n#include \"engine.h\"\r\n\r\nvoid _per_physics_tick_allocation_warning(StringName p_class_name, uint64_t &r_consecutive_allocs, uint64_t &r_last_alloc_tick)\r\n{\r\nif (Engine::get_singleton()->get_physics_frames()\r\nBLAH BLAH\r\n}\r\n```\r\n(It also depends where the bottlenecks are of course, but this is just an idea. As long as the class name is passed cheaply, and any namespace collisions are sorted for local variables (various ways around if that is a problem)).\r\n","created_at":"2026-10-14T08:55:48Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T09:16:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123663#discussion_r4268719836","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123663","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/4268719836"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123663#discussion_r4268719836"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123663"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/4268719836/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,